===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc}} {{term|σῆψις|tr=sepsis|lang=grc||putrefaction}} < {{term|σήπειν|lang=grc||to make rotten}} < {{term|σήψ|tr=seps|lang=grc||a kind of lizard, also a kind of serpent whose bite was alleged to cause putrefaction}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sepses}}

# {{pathology}} A serious medical [[condition]] in which the whole body is inflamed, and a known or suspected infection is present.

